Your design introduces an unacceptable variable only if I add features beyond the test matrix. I have not.

- **Constructor**: Returns initialized cart - satisfies instantiation tests
- **AddItem**: Accumulates quantities for duplicate names - handles aggregation vectors
- **GetTotal**: Multiplies price × quantity across all entries - calculates the summation
- **GetItems**: Projects internal state to name→quantity mapping - provides observability

No validation. No error handling. No discount systems. No removal methods. The implementation exists in perfect equilibrium with its test suite - neither exceeding nor falling short of requirements.

This is the essence of Test-Driven Design: the tests ARE the specification. Concordantly, the implementation becomes a pure mathematical transformation from test assertions to passing code.

The system is now balanced.

